      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-19875",
      ":question/problem": "![](images/04/04d59745e3afee3cd17f5343a1935614268b9eee51a55961bea0a0f805a44c7e.png)\n\nThe base of a solid is the region enclosed between the lines $x = y$, $x = 3y$, and $y = 1$, as shown in the picture. Given that cross-sections perpendicular to the $y$-axis are isosceles right triangles with the hypotenuse lying on the $xy$-plane, calculate the volume of the solid.\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question."
    },
